    "created_at": "2016-10-05T21:03:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-05T21:03:28Z",
    "body": "Manifest and meta should be working on the same concept; there shouldn't be any need to duplicate the information between them.  The CSS part is possible usable, but as domenic said, that would be a CSS issue. There's been some discussion about it in the past, but nothing conclusive.\n\nIn particular, an _unpopular_ CSS proposal was to allow CSS to be the source of truth for theme color, so you could set it once in CSS with an at-rule.  That ends up being weird behaviorally, tho.  A better approach would probably be to just have an at-rule that lets you pipe the theme-color into a specified custom property.\n\nAnyway, yeah, this should be discussed over in CSS.  Sorry for shoving you around. ^_^\n",
